# Optional: only for `python software\recording forecast` (occupancy forecasts precomputed into replays, shown in
# the viewer's bus chart). Install it in its own environment, not the main one (PyTorch alone is a few hundred MB).
# From the repository root:
#   uv venv .venv-forecast --python 3.12
#   uv pip install --python .venv-forecast -r software\recording\requirements-forecast.in
# Without uv: python -m venv .venv-forecast, then .venv-forecast\Scripts\python -m pip install -r <this file>
# The forecast command itself needs only the standard library, numpy, tzdata and Timestral (which brings PyTorch).

# Timestral 1.0.0 (not on PyPI), pinned to a commit. Code: Apache-2.0; model weights: Modified MIT.
timestral @ git+https://github.com/mistralai/timestral.git@a534bdbd244d64f3d9d743f46c7bf6fc330ed4ff
numpy
tzdata
